---
import CapabilityRegistry from '../components/CapabilityRegistry.astro';
import ImpactDemo from '../components/ImpactDemo.astro';
import CapabilityEvolutionLab from '../components/CapabilityEvolutionLab.astro';
import telemetry from '../data/telemetry_source.json';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f6f2e9" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Capability Lab is Lucas Mateus's independent human-AI R&D space: a practical exploration of learning, evidence, judgment and reusable capability."
    />
    <title>Capability Lab — Human + AI R&D by Lucas Mateus</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="masthead">
      <a class="brand" href="#home" aria-label="Capability Lab home">
        <span class="brand-mark">C</span>
        <span>C Lab</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="#system">Why it exists</a>
        <a href="#impact-demo">Try it</a>
        <a href="#experiment">Experiment</a>
        <a href="#evidence">Evidence</a>
        <a href="#capabilities">Technical details</a>
      </nav>
      <a class="portfolio-link" href="./portfolio/">Lucas's portfolio ↗</a>
    </header>

    <main id="home">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="hero-kicker">Lucas Mateus · Independent human + AI research</p>
          <h1 id="home-title">Can AI help us become more capable, not just faster?</h1>
          <p class="hero-intro">
            Capability Lab is my personal R&D space for exploring that question through practical experiments.
            I use AI, evidence and human judgment together — then keep what actually survives testing.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions" aria-label="Explore Capability Lab">
            <a class="primary-action" href="#impact-demo">Try a simple example ↓</a>
            <a class="secondary-action" href="#system">Why I built this</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="hero-note" aria-label="About Lucas and Capability Lab">
          <img
            src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/322756565?v=4&s=164"
            alt="Lucas Mateus"
            width="82"
            height="82"
            loading="lazy"
            fetchpriority="low"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <div>
            <span>ABOUT THE PERSON BEHIND THE LAB</span>
            <p>
              My background is in Talent Acquisition, Learning & Development and customer-facing work.
              I came to AI through curiosity about people, learning and better ways to work — not through a traditional software-engineering path.
            </p>
            <a href="./portfolio/">See my professional background ↗</a>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="story-section" id="system" aria-labelledby="story-title">
        <header class="story-head">
          <span>01 / WHY THIS EXISTS</span>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">A question became a lab</p>
            <h2 id="story-title">I did not want AI to become another tool I used without understanding what it changed in me.</h2>
          </div>
        </header>

        <div class="story-grid">
          <div class="story-copy">
            <p class="lead">
              The more I worked with AI, the more interesting question stopped being “what can the model do?”
              and became “what can a person learn to do with it?”
            </p>
            <p>
              C Lab is where I test ways of making AI-assisted work more understandable, reviewable and reusable.
              Sometimes that means better prompts. Often it means something less glamorous: clearer goals, explicit assumptions,
              stronger evidence, a useful failure record, or a human checkpoint before calling something done.
            </p>
            <p>
              The aim is not to remove human judgment. It is to make the collaboration between human judgment and machine capability
              easier to inspect, improve and carry forward.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="question-stack" aria-label="Questions Capability Lab explores">
            <article>
              <span>01</span>
              <p>Can AI help someone learn from experience instead of only producing an answer?</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span>02</span>
              <p>Can good work become reusable capability instead of disappearing inside a chat?</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span>03</span>
              <p>Can evidence and human review make AI-assisted work easier to trust?</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span>04</span>
              <p>Can useful capability survive when the underlying model or provider changes?</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="method-title">
        <header>
          <span>02 / THE BASIC LOOP</span>
          <h2 id="method-title">Ask. Try. Check. Keep what works.</h2>
          <p>
            Most of the Lab can be understood through four ordinary actions. The technical architecture exists to support this loop,
            not to be the story itself.
          </p>
        </header>

        <ol class="method-loop">
          <li>
            <span>01</span>
            <strong>Ask</strong>
            <p>Start with a real problem or uncertainty worth resolving.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>02</span>
            <strong>Try</strong>
            <p>Build the smallest useful way to test an approach.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>03</span>
            <strong>Check</strong>
            <p>Separate what worked from what merely looked convincing.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>04</span>
            <strong>Keep</strong>
            <p>Preserve validated learning so future work can start from a better place.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <ImpactDemo />
      <CapabilityEvolutionLab />

      <section class="evidence-section" id="evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
        <header class="section-head">
          <span>05 / WHAT COUNTS AS PROGRESS</span>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Evidence before confidence</p>
            <h2 id="evidence-title">A polished answer is not the same thing as a learned capability.</h2>
          </div>
        </header>

        <div class="evidence-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="number">A</span>
            <h3>Show the evidence</h3>
            <p>
              A claim should point to something inspectable: a test, an artifact, a comparison, a result or a clearly stated limitation.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="number">B</span>
            <h3>Keep humans in the loop</h3>
            <p>
              AI can structure, challenge and accelerate work. Important conclusions still need human judgment and explicit review.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="number">C</span>
            <h3>Learn from failure</h3>
            <p>
              A failed experiment is useful when it reduces uncertainty and changes what happens next. Hiding failure would make the Lab less useful.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="number">D</span>
            <h3>Do not confuse “built” with “proven”</h3>
            <p>
              Experiments, candidates and validated capabilities are different states. The public surface keeps those boundaries visible.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="technical-section" id="capabilities" aria-labelledby="technical-title">
        <header class="technical-head">
          <div>
            <span>06 / FOR THE CURIOUS</span>
            <p class="eyebrow">Technical details, when you want them</p>
            <h2 id="technical-title">The machinery sits underneath the story.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            This is the same evidence-backed system surface that existed before this redesign.
            It is intentionally lower on the page so a visitor can understand the purpose of C Lab before meeting its internal vocabulary.
            Public presentation layer only; no runtime authority.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="metric-band" aria-label="Current system metrics">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <strong>{telemetry.summary.materialized_candidate_count}</strong>
            <p>Materialized capabilities</p>
            <code>evidence-backed · evaluation required</code>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <strong>{telemetry.summary.scaffold_unverified_count}</strong>
            <p>Scaffold / unverified</p>
            <code>not promoted by appearance</code>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <strong>{telemetry.summary.current_tier}</strong>
            <p>Verification depth</p>
            <code>current candidate tier</code>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>04</span>
            <strong>{telemetry.operator.level}</strong>
            <p>Operator consolidation</p>
            <code>{telemetry.operator.label}</code>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="boundary-note">
          <div>
            <span>PUBLIC</span>
            <p>High-level capability names, coarse maturity state, verification tier and sanitized publication metadata.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span>PRIVATE</span>
            <p>Execution receipts, credentials, internal evidence, implementation contracts and canonical working state.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="registry-wrap">
          <CapabilityRegistry />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="tier-section" id="progress" aria-labelledby="progress-title">
        <div class="tier-copy">
          <span>07 / VERIFICATION DEPTH</span>
          <h2 id="progress-title">Progress without pretending every stage is finished.</h2>
          <p>
            These levels describe how deeply a capability has been checked. They are tracking states, not a score for the person behind the Lab.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ol class="tier-list">
          {telemetry.tiers.map((tier, index) => (
            <li class:list={[tier.state === 'active_candidate' && 'is-current', tier.state === 'sealed' && 'is-done']}>
              <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <b>{tier.id}</b>
              <em>{tier.label}</em>
              <small>{tier.state}</small>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="closing-section" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
        <span>THE SHORT VERSION</span>
        <h2 id="closing-title">C Lab is a place to turn curiosity into tested learning — and tested learning into capability that can be reused.</h2>
        <div>
          <a class="primary-action" href="#impact-demo">Try the example ↑</a>
          <a class="secondary-action" href="./portfolio/">Meet Lucas through his work ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer class="footer">
        <div>
          <span>Capability Lab · Lucas Mateus</span>
          <span>Independent applied R&D · selective public surface</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <a href="./portfolio/">Professional portfolio</a>
          <a href="#home">Back to top ↑</a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root{
    --ink:#171613;
    --paper:#f6f2e9;
    --paper-deep:#ece5d7;
    --surface:#fffdf8;
    --line:#cfc7b8;
    --muted:#6f6a61;
    --green:#176b52;
    --green-soft:#dfece5;
    --blue:#315aa8;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box}
  html{scroll-behavior:smooth;background:var(--paper)}
  body{
    margin:0;
    background:var(--paper);
    color:var(--ink);
    font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
  }
  a{color:inherit}
  .masthead{
    position:sticky;
    top:0;
    z-index:20;
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:66px;
    padding:0 28px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);
    background:rgba(246,242,233,.94);
    backdrop-filter:blur(12px);
  }
  .brand{
    display:inline-flex;
    align-items:center;
    gap:10px;
    width:max-content;
    text-decoration:none;
    font-size:12px;
    font-weight:700;
    letter-spacing:.01em;
  }
  .brand-mark{
    display:grid;
    place-items:center;
    width:30px;
    height:30px;
    border:1px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius:50%;
    font:700 11px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;
  }
  .masthead nav{display:flex;gap:22px}
  .masthead nav a,.portfolio-link{
    text-decoration:none;
    font-size:11px;
    color:#5f5a52;
  }
  .masthead nav a:hover,.portfolio-link:hover{color:var(--ink)}
  .portfolio-link{justify-self:end;font-weight:700}
  main{width:min(100%,1600px);margin:0 auto;padding:0 28px 42px}

  .hero{
    min-height:calc(100vh - 66px);
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.35fr) minmax(300px,.65fr);
    gap:70px;
    align-items:end;
    padding:72px 0 52px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .hero-copy{align-self:center}
  .hero-kicker,.story-head>span,.method-section>header>span,.section-head>span,.technical-head>div>span,.tier-copy>span,.closing-section>span{
    font:600 10px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.08em;
    color:var(--muted);
  }
  .hero h1{
    max-width:1100px;
    margin:26px 0 28px;
    font-size:clamp(68px,8.8vw,138px);
    line-height:.88;
    letter-spacing:-.075em;
    font-weight:500;
  }
  .hero-intro{
    max-width:760px;
    margin:0;
    font-size:clamp(20px,2vw,30px);
    line-height:1.34;
    letter-spacing:-.025em;
    color:#3f3c36;
  }
  .hero-actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:34px}
  .primary-action,.secondary-action{
    display:inline-flex;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    min-height:46px;
    padding:0 17px;
    text-decoration:none;
    font-size:12px;
    font-weight:700;
  }
  .primary-action{background:var(--ink);color:#fff}
  .primary-action:hover{background:var(--green)}
  .secondary-action{border:1px solid #9c958a}
  .secondary-action:hover{border-color:var(--ink);background:var(--surface)}
  .hero-note{
    align-self:end;
    margin-bottom:4px;
    padding:24px;
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:18px;
    background:rgba(255,253,248,.72);
  }
  .hero-note img{
    width:82px;
    height:82px;
    border-radius:50%;
    object-fit:cover;
    filter:grayscale(.15);
  }
  .hero-note>div{margin-top:28px}
  .hero-note span,.eyebrow{
    font:600 9px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.08em;
    color:var(--green);
  }
  .hero-note p{margin:12px 0 18px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:#4d4942}
  .hero-note a{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #918a7e;padding-bottom:3px}

  .story-section,.method-section,.evidence-section,.technical-section,.tier-section,.closing-section{
    padding:88px 0;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .story-head,.section-head{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:220px 1fr;
    gap:38px;
    align-items:start;
    margin-bottom:58px;
  }
  .story-head h2,.section-head h2,.technical-head h2,.tier-copy h2,.closing-section h2{
    max-width:1150px;
    margin:12px 0 0;
    font-size:clamp(44px,6vw,86px);
    line-height:.96;
    letter-spacing:-.06em;
    font-weight:500;
  }
  .story-grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(360px,.75fr);
    gap:90px;
    margin-left:258px;
  }
  .story-copy{max-width:720px}
  .story-copy p{margin:0 0 22px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:#514d46}
  .story-copy .lead{font-size:24px;line-height:1.44;letter-spacing:-.025em;color:var(--ink)}
  .question-stack{border-top:1px solid var(--ink)}
  .question-stack article{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:48px 1fr;
    gap:20px;
    padding:20px 0;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .question-stack span{
    font:600 10px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;
    color:var(--green);
  }
  .question-stack p{margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.42}

  .method-section>header{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:220px minmax(0,1fr) minmax(260px,.55fr);
    gap:38px;
    align-items:start;
    margin-bottom:52px;
  }
  .method-section h2{margin:0;font-size:clamp(46px,5.8vw,82px);line-height:.96;letter-spacing:-.06em;font-weight:500}
  .method-section>header>p{margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#555048}
  .method-loop{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;border-top:1px solid var(--ink)}
  .method-loop li{min-height:270px;padding:22px 28px 28px 0;border-right:1px solid var(--line)}
  .method-loop li+li{padding-left:28px}
  .method-loop li:last-child{border-right:0}
  .method-loop span{font:600 10px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:var(--green)}
  .method-loop strong{display:block;margin:58px 0 14px;font-size:34px;letter-spacing:-.04em}
  .method-loop p{max-width:260px;margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.65;color:#5d5850}

  .section-head .eyebrow{margin:0}
  .evidence-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);border-top:1px solid var(--ink)}
  .evidence-grid article{min-height:300px;padding:24px 28px 30px 0;border-right:1px solid var(--line)}
  .evidence-grid article+article{padding-left:28px}
  .evidence-grid article:last-child{border-right:0}
  .number{font:600 10px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:var(--green)}
  .evidence-grid h3{margin:58px 0 16px;font-size:28px;letter-spacing:-.035em}
  .evidence-grid p{margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;color:#5a554e}

  .technical-section{background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(236,229,215,.45),transparent 55%)}
  .technical-head{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(300px,.55fr);
    gap:80px;
    align-items:end;
    margin-bottom:54px;
  }
  .technical-head>p{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#514d46}
  .metric-band{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}
  .metric-band article{min-height:190px;padding:18px 20px 22px 0;border-right:1px solid var(--line)}
  .metric-band article+article{padding-left:20px}
  .metric-band article:last-child{border-right:0}
  .metric-band span{font:600 9px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#777168}
  .metric-band strong{display:block;margin-top:24px;font-size:clamp(48px,5.5vw,82px);line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.06em;font-weight:500}
  .metric-band p{margin:18px 0 5px;font-size:12px}
  .metric-band code{font:500 9px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#79736a}
  .boundary-note{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}
  .boundary-note>div{padding:24px 28px 24px 0;border-right:1px solid var(--line)}
  .boundary-note>div+div{padding-left:28px;border-right:0}
  .boundary-note span{font:700 9px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:var(--green);letter-spacing:.08em}
  .boundary-note p{max-width:600px;margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#59544c}
  .registry-wrap{padding-top:50px}

  .tier-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.85fr 1.15fr;gap:70px}
  .tier-copy h2{font-size:clamp(42px,5vw,72px)}
  .tier-copy p{max-width:560px;margin:22px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:#58534b}
  .tier-list{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;border-top:1px solid var(--ink)}
  .tier-list li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:48px 56px 1fr auto;align-items:center;gap:18px;min-height:72px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .tier-list li span{font:600 9px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#858078}
  .tier-list li b{font-size:14px}
  .tier-list li em{font-style:normal;font-size:13px}
  .tier-list li small{font:600 9px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;color:#757068}
  .tier-list li.is-current b,.tier-list li.is-current small{color:var(--green)}
  .tier-list li.is-current{border-bottom-color:#91b9a8}
  .tier-list li.is-done{color:#383631}

  .closing-section{text-align:center;padding-left:7vw;padding-right:7vw}
  .closing-section h2{margin:18px auto 34px;max-width:1200px}
  .closing-section>div{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}

  .footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:30px;padding:24px 0 0}
  .footer div{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .footer span,.footer a{
    font:600 9px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.05em;
    color:#69645c;
  }
  .footer a{text-decoration:none}

  @media(max-width:1080px){
    .masthead{grid-template-columns:1fr auto}
    .masthead nav{display:none}
    .hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;min-height:auto;padding-top:84px}
    .hero-note{max-width:620px}
    .story-grid{margin-left:0}
    .method-section>header{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .technical-head{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .evidence-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
    .evidence-grid article:nth-child(2){border-right:0}
    .evidence-grid article:nth-child(-n+2){border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  }
  @media(max-width:860px){
    .story-head,.section-head{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px}
    .story-grid,.tier-section{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .metric-band{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
    .metric-band article:nth-child(2){border-right:0}
    .metric-band article:nth-child(-n+2){border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .method-loop{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
    .method-loop li:nth-child(2){border-right:0}
    .method-loop li:nth-child(-n+2){border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  }
  @media(max-width:640px){
    .masthead{padding:0 18px}
    .portfolio-link{font-size:10px}
    main{padding:0 18px 32px}
    .hero{padding:58px 0 42px;gap:42px}
    .hero h1{font-size:clamp(56px,18vw,88px);line-height:.9}
    .hero-intro{font-size:20px}
    .hero-note{padding:20px}
    .hero-actions,.closing-section>div{align-items:stretch;flex-direction:column}
    .primary-action,.secondary-action{width:100%}
    .story-section,.method-section,.evidence-section,.technical-section,.tier-section,.closing-section{padding:58px 0}
    .story-grid{gap:42px}
    .story-copy .lead{font-size:20px}
    .method-loop,.evidence-grid,.metric-band,.boundary-note{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .method-loop li,.method-loop li+li,.evidence-grid article,.evidence-grid article+article,.metric-band article,.metric-band article+article{
